/*
# Button

A labeled action control. The action is its `onClick` — write it at the use site
exactly as on any View; `Button` adds the interaction states, the themed look, and
keyboard activation (Space/Enter drives the same `onClick`). `primary = true` fills
with the accent; the default is the quiet control look.

```declare-fragment
Button [ label = "Save" ]
Button [ label = "Delete", iconLeft = "TrashIcon" ]
Button [ label = "Options", menu = { app.optionsMenu } ]      // chevron implied
Button [ iconLeft = "CloseIcon" ]                             // icon only
```

Three slots in a row — `iconLeft`, the label, `iconRight` — laid out by
`SimpleLayout` and sized from `contentWidth`, so an absent label or icon costs
nothing and needs no special case: an invisible child is skipped and its space
reclaimed. A `menu` supplies the right icon on its own (`control.declare`).

The fill walks the four-rung ladder — `control` at rest, `controlHover`,
`controlPressed`, and `controlSelected` while its menu is open. Before the ladder
existed this read `down || hot ? controlActive : control`, which meant **hovering
a button looked exactly like pressing it**.
*/

include [ "control.declare", "icons/icon.declare" ]

class Button extends Control [
    height = { typeof theme.buttonHeight == "number" ? theme.buttonHeight : 40 },
    cornerRadius = { typeof theme.buttonRadius == "number" ? Math.min(theme.buttonRadius, height / 2) : theme.controlRadius },
    label:   string = "",
    primary: boolean = false,

    iconSize = 18,
    gap:  number = 8,
    padH: number = 16,

    onClick() { },
    press()   { flashPress(); if (menu != null) openMenu(); onClick() },

    // one ink decision, so a primary button's icon and its label agree

    inkColor: Color = { primary ? theme.accentText : theme.text },
    textColor = { inkColor },

    // The RUN sizes to its own content and centres itself in the button; the
    // button's default width is the run plus symmetric padding. Two objects, so
    // the two facts stay independent: a button given an explicit `width` (a
    // dialog's equal-width row, a toolbar's fixed slot) still centres what it
    // holds, which a packed layout on the button itself would not.
    //
    // Not flexing Spacers: SimpleLayout reads the view's own extent to divide
    // slack, and the extent here is derived FROM the content — that closes a
    // cycle. A self-sizing child breaks it, because the run's width never looks
    // outward.

    width   = { this.run.width + this.padH * 2 },
    opacity = { disabled ? 0.45 : 1 },

    fill = { primary   ? theme.accent
           : menuOpen  ? theme.controlSelected
           : down      ? theme.controlPressed
           : hot       ? theme.controlHover
           :             theme.control },

    // platforms whose secondary buttons are BORDERED say so in the theme
    // (Cupertino's hairline, Fluent's 1px) — flat systems leave it null

    stroke  = { !primary && theme.buttonBorder != null ? stroke(1, theme.buttonBorder) : null },

    run: View [ height = { parent.height },
        x = { (parent.width - this.width) / 2 },
        width = { this.contentWidth },
        layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = x, spacing = { classroot.gap } ],

        ico:   IconHost [ kind = { classroot.iconLeft },  ink = { classroot.inkColor } ],
        cap:   Text [ y = center, wrap = false, fontWeight = semibold,
            visible = { classroot.label != "" }, text = { classroot.label } ],
        trail: IconHost [ kind = { classroot.rightIcon }, ink = { classroot.inkColor } ]
        ]
    ]
